I replaced the linear scan with a one-time-initialized direct lookup table indexed by message number, so each call becomes a single array access instead of scanning `mesgs`. The table preserves the original first-match behavior for duplicate message numbers.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* table[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
        {
            if (table[mesgs[i].num] == nullptr)
                table[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        initialized = true;
    }

    return table[num];
}
```